// GalHack's item catalogue: everything that sits in a storage or a pocket. Blocks are not items:
// placing a block costs its bill (blocks.json) straight from the structure's shared storage.
//
//   category  raw (mined, dug or harvested), unique (found only), refined (made from raw only),
//             part, component, consumable, ammo, tool
//   rarity    the design's five-step ladder: common, uncommon, rare, exotic, unique. A crafted
//             item is never rarer-looking than it is: its rarity is at least that of every input.
//   source    raw and unique items only: mine (a deposit), dig (any rock), harvest (plants and
//             creatures), explore (POIs, wrecks, derelicts: unique finds, never mined)
//   mass      kg per unit
//   volume    storage units (SU, a litre) per unit: a small cargo block holds 125 SU, a large 8,000
//   deposit   raw only: the deposit kind the planet generator places today, if any
//   fuel      fuel units per item (section 13 of the design)
//   rounds    ammo only: rounds in one box, belt or rack. Storage, the constructor and the restock
//             threshold all count boxes, so the three always agree.
//   restock   ammo only: the default auto-restock threshold, in boxes
//   stack     units one inventory slot holds (default by category: raw and refined 500, parts 200,
//             components 50, consumables and ammo 25, unique 10, tools 1)
//   unlock    its tech-tree node: the level it unlocks from, its point cost, its parent node (an item
//             id or block@grid) and its tab. Materials and parts have none: they are always made.
//
// Names: plain words and real metals for common goods, crystal and star-metal names for rare
// ones, lost-technology names for unique finds. Every name is GalHack's own.
